{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774535186,"nonce":"ykRPMSLJgjoHVnAZeFRBEzq+Qbk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM73B5BD","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/15","origin":"github"},"title":"Create boat deployment manifest with gitcloud URLs","message":"## Summary\n\nSet up `unh_echoboats_project11` as a manifest repo for boat deployments, with `.repos` files pointing at gitcloud (`git@gitcloud:field/`) and scoped to the layers needed on the boat.\n\nPart of #14 (Deploy project11 on BizzyBoat).\n\nSee also: [#13 comment on manifest scope](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/13#issuecomment-4128942561) and [note on repo duplication](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/13#issuecomment-4128944654).\n\n## Layers Needed on Boat\n\n- `underlay_ws` — additional dependencies\n- `core_ws` — marine autonomy core\n- `platforms_ws` — echoboat packages (including this repo)\n- `site_ws` — private site config (credentials, hosts, network)\n\nSimulation and UI layers are **not** needed on the boat.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Add `config/` directory with `layers.txt` and `optional_layers.txt`\n- [ ] Add `config/repos/` with `.repos` files for each layer, pointing at gitcloud URLs\n- [ ] Add `config/bootstrap.yaml` (Pattern B, `layer: platforms`)\n- [ ] Verify the workspace can bootstrap from this manifest (on a test machine or in a worktree)\n- [ ] Document how to use this manifest for boat deployments\n\n## Note on Repo Duplication\n\nThe `.repos` files will duplicate content from `unh_marine_autonomy` (the main workspace manifest). This is intentional — each manifest should be self-contained so boat workspaces don't need to cross-reference another manifest. If drift becomes a maintenance burden, revisit with an include mechanism.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}